---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
const curl = 'curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dipeshdulal/gothalo/main/install.sh | sh';
---

<section class="wrap sec rule-top stack" id="install">
  <h2 class="h2 display">Install.</h2>
  <div>
    <div class="install">
      <div class="istep">
        <h3 class="display">Herdr agent integration</h3>
        <div class="istep__body">
          <p>
            Run this on the Herdr host for every agent you use, or the transcript view shows
            one agent's conversation under another.
          </p>
          <pre class="block"><code>herdr integration install claude
herdr integration install codex
herdr integration install gemini
herdr integration install hermes
herdr integration install opencode</code></pre>
          <p>
            One line per agent kind.{' '}
            <a href={`${base}docs/guides/agent-integration/`}>Agent integration</a> lists where
            each one keeps its transcript.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="istep">
        <h3 class="display">The bridge</h3>
        <div class="istep__body">
          <p>macOS or Linux, from the latest release:</p>
          <div class="cmd">
            <span class="cmd__prompt" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <code class="cmd__text" id="install-cmd-2">{curl}</code>
            <button
              class="cmd__copy"
              type="button"
              data-copy="install-cmd-2"
              aria-label="Copy the install command"
            >
              <svg
                class="copy"
                width="16"
                height="16"
                viewBox="0 0 16 16"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.5"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <rect x="5" y="5" width="9" height="9" rx="1.5"></rect>
                <path d="M11 5V3.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 9.5 2h-6A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 2 3.5v6A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 3.5 11H5"
                ></path>
              </svg>
              <svg
                class="check"
                width="16"
                height="16"
                viewBox="0 0 16 16"
                fill="none"
                stroke="currentColor"
                stroke-width="1.5"
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path d="M3 8.5 6.5 12 13 4.5"></path>
              </svg>
            </button>
          </div>
          <p>
            The script detects your OS and architecture, downloads the matching release
            archive, and verifies its SHA-256 against the release's checksums.txt before
            installing. That check is best effort: it needs shasum or sha256sum on the host
            and a checksums.txt on the release. From source instead:
          </p>
          <pre class="block"><code>go install github.com/dipeshdulal/gothalo/cmd/gothalo@latest</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="istep">
        <h3 class="display">Run it and pair a phone</h3>
        <div class="istep__body">
          <pre class="block"><code>gothalo serve            <span class="comment"># writes config.json and an admin token</span>
gothalo-service install  <span class="comment"># supervise via launchd or systemd</span>
gothalo pair             <span class="comment"># a one-time QR, about a 5 minute TTL</span></code></pre>
          <p>
            It defaults to <span class="mono">127.0.0.1:8787</span>. Point it at the tailnet
            so the phone can reach it:
          </p>
          <pre class="block"><code>GOTHALO_ADDR=$(tailscale ip -4):8787 \
GOTHALO_PUBLIC_URL=https://&lt;host&gt;.&lt;tailnet&gt;.ts.net:8787 \
gothalo serve</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="istep">
        <h3 class="display">The app</h3>
        <div class="istep__body">
          <p>
            Android, no packaged APK yet. Point it at your own Firebase project first, then
            build it:
          </p>
          <pre class="block"><code>./scripts/setup-firebase.sh --project &lt;firebase-project-id&gt;
cd app && flutter pub get && flutter build apk --release</code></pre>
          <p>
            Or skip the build entirely and{' '}
            <a href={`${base}app/`}>open the web app</a> — the same client, hosted, pairing
            with your bridge (<a href="#web-app">how that works</a>). A bridge built with{' '}
            <span class="mono">./scripts/build.sh</span> also bakes the app in and serves it
            as a PWA from its own URL, the same address the app pairs to. The install.sh
            binary does not include the web UI yet.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="istep">
        <h3 class="display">Push, when you want it</h3>
        <div class="istep__body">
          <p>
            Without credentials the bridge logs instead of notifying. Two steps turn it on,
            credentials for the bridge and a Firebase project for the app:
          </p>
          <pre class="block"><code>gothalo push login --project &lt;firebase-project-id&gt;
./scripts/setup-firebase.sh --project &lt;firebase-project-id&gt;</code></pre>
          <p>
            The full walkthrough, including why every fork needs its own project, is in the{' '}
            <a href={`${base}docs/guides/push/`}>push guide</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="note">
      The complete walkthrough, with config, env overrides and revoking a device, is at{' '}
      <a href={`${base}docs/install/`}>Install</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
